cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Nayancode Workbench in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Nayancode Workbench: open-source bioinformatics and cheminformatics in the web browser"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Vivofold"
    website: "https://vivofold.in"
    email: "support@vivofold.in"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/balajimadhvn/nayancode"
url: "https://balajimadhvn.github.io/nayancode/"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - cheminformatics
  - webassembly
  - rna-seq
  - single-cell
  - phylogenetics
  - privacy
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  The Nayancode Workbench is a free, open-source collection of analysis studios that run entirely in the web
  browser: sequence analysis and cloning, read mapping with minimap2 and samtools compiled to WebAssembly,
  variant interpretation, bulk RNA-seq differential expression and enrichment, single-cell clustering,
  microbiome diversity, cheminformatics and QSAR, protein structure analysis and maximum-likelihood
  phylogenetics. Input files are analysed on the user's own computer, and every result records its own
  provenance and methods text.
